# row's run_id is derived from the log (the launch stamp mr-launch.sh writes on its ATTEMPT=1
# line), so it names the session rather than the caller: a slice that is relaunched or resumed
# gets one row per session, and the same session offered twice (the tick's reconcile, mr-spawn
# at relaunch, a retry after a timeout) is written once. Cost, attempts and model come from
# mr-cost-sum, which reports the session's own spend from a counter that is cumulative across
# `--resume`, and falls back on the session transcript when the log reports less.
run_log=a.get("from-log")
